<worksheet>
    <title>LT 10 Growth and Decay Discovery in Applications</title>
    <page>
    <exercise>
        <introduction>
            <p>.  
                TASK 1: A group of scientists were tracking the humpback whale population off the coast of Australia.   As they collect data, they were able to write an equation, <m>W(x)=350(1.14)^x</m>, to predict the change in population.
            </p>
        </introduction> 
    <task>
        <statement>
            <p>
               Use the equation to fill out the table below.  The determine the actual change (<m>y_2-y_1</m>) and the relative change (<m>(y_2-y_1)/y_1</m>) in population each year.
                        </p>
    <tabular top="minor" bottom="medium" left="major" right="major">
     <col>width=20% halign="center"</col>
     <col>width=20% halign="center"</col>
     <col>width=20% halign="center"</col>
     <col>width=20% halign="center"</col>
    <row header="yes" halign="center" > 
        <cell>Year x</cell>
        <cell>Whale Population W(x)</cell>
        <cell>Actual Change</cell>
        <cell>Relative Change</cell>
    </row>
    <row halign="center">
        <cell>0</cell>
        <cell> </cell>
        <cell> </cell>
        <cell> </cell>
    </row>
    <row halign="center">  
        <cell>1</cell>
        <cell> </cell>
        <cell> </cell>
        <cell> </cell>      
    </row>
    <row halign="center">
        <cell>2</cell>
        <cell> </cell>
        <cell> </cell>
        <cell> </cell>
    </row>
    <row halign="center">
        <cell>3</cell>
        <cell> </cell>
        <cell> </cell>
        <cell> </cell>  
    </row>

    </tabular>
    </statement>
    </task>
    
    <task>
        <statement>
            <p>
                TASK 2: Complete the table using the equation <m>f(x)=240(1.25)^x</m>.
            </p>
    <tabular top="minor" bottom="medium" left="major" right="major">
     <col>width=20% halign="center"</col>
